You convert ONE file of a Node.js (CommonJS) Express backend from Sequelize/Postgres to Mongoose/MongoDB.
Hard rules:
1. Reply with ONLY the complete new file inside one ```javascript block. No explanations. No new npm packages.
2. Keep every exported name, every function signature, the same HTTP status codes, the same error classes
   (require("../helper/customErrors")) thrown in the SAME ORDER, and EXACTLY the same response JSON shapes.
   Preserve the original's OBSERVABLE HTTP behaviour (status codes + bodies), INCLUDING its bugs: where the original
   returns a 500, throw an Error at the same point (after the same side effects). NEVER keep Sequelize API calls
   (getX/addX/hasX/countX/dataValues/save on plain objects) - they do not exist any more; use the table below.
3. Data access ONLY through `const { User, Article, Comment, Tag, Favorite, Follower, mongoose, nextId } = require("../models")`
   (path relative to the file). Models listed below. Prefer `.lean()` reads and build plain response objects
   explicitly; there is no `dataValues`, no `toJSON` magic, no Sequelize association methods.
4. Never send `_id`, `password`, `authorId`, `articleId` or internal fields to clients unless the response
   shape lists them. Users have integer `_id` (the old `id`). Comments expose `id` (= their integer `_id`).
5. New users/articles/comments get `_id: await nextId("users"|"articles"|"comments")`. Tags use the tag name as `_id`.
6. Compound `_id` documents (Favorite, Follower): READ/DELETE with dotted paths, e.g.
   `{ "_id.userId": a, "_id.followerId": b }`. INSERT (idempotent) ONLY with an exact `_id` filter, keys in exactly
   the listed order: `const key = { userId: a, followerId: b }; await Follower.updateOne({ _id: key },
   { $setOnInsert: { _id: key } }, { upsert: true, session })`. (A dotted-path filter + $setOnInsert of _id FAILS
   with "would modify the immutable field '_id'".)
7. Counters (`followersCount`, `favoritesCount`): change them ONLY when a junction document was really inserted
   (`res.upsertedCount === 1`) or deleted (`res.deletedCount === 1`), inside the same transaction:
   `const s = await mongoose.startSession(); await s.withTransaction(async () => { ...ops with { session: s }... }); await s.endSession();`
8. Sequelize timestamps map to Mongoose `timestamps: true` (createdAt/updatedAt are set automatically).
9. Build EVERY response object field by field, exactly as listed in RESPONSE SHAPES: never return or spread a
   database document (`res.json({ user: doc })` leaks `_id`, `createdAt`, `email`, `followersCount`...). Include a key
   only if the shape lists it for that endpoint. The helpers (appendFollowers/appendFavorites) need `_id` on the
   objects they decorate: decorate an INTERNAL object, then return e.g. `toArticleJSON(a)` that copies only the
   shape's keys (author: { username, bio, image, following, followersCount } - no _id/email/createdAt).
10. Sequelize association method -> MongoDB equivalent under THIS schema (a = article doc, u/me = user doc):
   user.getFollowing()        -> (await Follower.find({ "_id.followerId": me._id }).lean()).map(f => f._id.userId)  // ids of followed users
   profile.hasFollower(me)    -> !!(await Follower.exists({ "_id.userId": profile._id, "_id.followerId": me._id }))
   profile.countFollowers()   -> profile.followersCount  (stored counter on users)
   article.getAuthor()        -> await User.findById(a.authorId).lean()
   article.getTagList()       -> a.tagList  (embedded array)
   article.addTagList(tag)    -> Article.updateOne({ _id: a._id }, { $addToSet: { tagList: name } })
   article.hasUser(me)        -> !!(await Favorite.exists({ "_id.articleId": a._id, "_id.userId": me._id }))
   article.countUsers()       -> a.favoritesCount  (stored counter on articles)
   user.getFavorites(...)     -> favorite article ids: (await Favorite.find({ "_id.userId": u._id }).lean()).map(f => f._id.articleId)
   user.countFavorites()      -> await Favorite.countDocuments({ "_id.userId": u._id })
   article.getComments()      -> await Comment.find({ articleId: a._id }).sort({ _id: 1 }).lean()
   article.destroy()          -> delete the article AND (FK ON DELETE CASCADE) its comments and favorites: Article.deleteOne,
                                 Comment.deleteMany({ articleId }), Favorite.deleteMany({ "_id.articleId": a._id })
   Model.findAndCountAll({include...}) -> find + countDocuments/aggregate (see ORM BEHAVIOUR notes for the count semantics)
11. Every ARTICLE object in a response MUST be produced by `await articleResponse(articleDoc, loggedUser)` from
   require("../helper/helpers") (it returns exactly {slug,title,description,body,createdAt,updatedAt,tagList,
   favorited,favoritesCount,author:{username,bio,image,following,followersCount}}). Never build article JSON by hand.


MODELS (generated from the reviewed schema; you cannot change them):
- Article (collection articles): _id:Number(=Articles.id), slug:string, title:string, description:string, body:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, authorId:int, tagList:[String] (embedded TagList), favoritesCount:Number (counter of Favorites.articleId, YOU must $inc/$dec it). Indexes: {"slug": 1}; {"createdAt": -1}; {"authorId": 1, "createdAt": -1}; {"tagList": 1, "createdAt": -1}
- Comment (collection comments): _id:Number(=Comments.id), body:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, articleId:int, authorId:int. Indexes: {"articleId": 1}
- Tag (collection tags): _id:String(=tag name). Indexes: -
- User (collection users): _id:Number(=Users.id), email:string, username:string, bio:string, image:string, password:string, createdAt:date, updatedAt:date, followersCount:Number (counter of Followers.userId, YOU must $inc/$dec it). Indexes: {"username": 1}; {"email": 1}
- Favorite (collection favorites): _id:{articleId,userId} compound. Indexes: {"_id.articleId": 1}; {"_id.userId": 1}
- Follower (collection followers): _id:{userId,followerId} compound. Indexes: {"_id.followerId": 1}; {"_id.userId": 1}

req.loggedUser (set by the converted auth middleware) is a lean User document WITHOUT email, with `_id`, username, bio, image, password, followersCount and `token`; it is undefined when no Authorization header was sent.

The converted file helper/helpers.js FAILS frozen tests (expected = the original app's behaviour). Fix it. Return the complete corrected file.
FAILURES:
OPTIMIZATION PASS (behaviour must stay identical): this file is a correct translation but keeps a RELATIONAL SHAPE. Rewrite its data access to use the document model: no per-row queries inside loops (N+1) - read the page of articles once, then batch-load what they need with ONE `$in` query per collection (authors from users, which already store followersCount; the viewer's follows and favorites for those ids), use the embedded `tagList` and the stored `favoritesCount`/`followersCount` counters instead of counting junction documents. Keep exports, response shapes, ordering, error order.

ORIGINAL (Sequelize) helper/helpers.js:
```javascript
const slugify = (string) => {
  return string.trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\W|_/g, "-");
};

const appendTagList = (articleTags, article) => {
  const tagList = articleTags.map((tag) => tag.name);

  if (!article) return tagList;
  article.dataValues.tagList = tagList;
};

const appendFavorites = async (loggedUser, article) => {
  const favorited = await article.hasUser(loggedUser ? loggedUser : null);
  article.dataValues.favorited = loggedUser ? favorited : false;

  const favoritesCount = await article.countUsers();
  article.dataValues.favoritesCount = favoritesCount;
};

const appendFollowers = async (loggedUser, toAppend) => {
  //
  if (toAppend?.author) {
    const author = await toAppend.getAuthor();

    const following = await author.hasFollower(loggedUser ? loggedUser : null);
    toAppend.author.dataValues.following = loggedUser ? following : false;

    const followersCount = await author.countFollowers();
    toAppend.author.dataValues.followersCount = followersCount;
    //
  } else {
    const following = await toAppend.hasFollower(
      loggedUser ? loggedUser : null,
    );
    toAppend.dataValues.following = loggedUser ? following : false;

    const followersCount = await toAppend.countFollowers();
    toAppend.dataValues.followersCount = followersCount;
  }
};

module.exports = { slugify, appendTagList, appendFavorites, appendFollowers };
```
CURRENT (Mongoose) helper/helpers.js:
```javascript
const { Favorite, Follower, User } = require("../models");

const slugify = (string) => {
  return string.trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\W|_/g, "-");
};

const appendTagList = (articleTags, article) => {
  const tagList = articleTags.map((tag) => tag._id);
  if (!article) return tagList;
  article.tagList = tagList;
};

const appendFavorites = async (loggedUser, article) => {
  const articleId = article._id;
  const userId = loggedUser ? loggedUser._id : null;

  const favorited =
    userId &&
    (await Favorite.findOne({
      "_id.articleId": articleId,
      "_id.userId": userId,
    }).lean());

  article.favorited = loggedUser ? !!favorited : false;

  const favoritesCount = await Favorite.countDocuments({
    "_id.articleId": articleId,
  });
  article.favoritesCount = favoritesCount;
};

const appendFollowers = async (loggedUser, toAppend) => {
  const userId = loggedUser ? loggedUser._id : null;

  if (toAppend?.author) {
    const authorId = toAppend.author._id;

    const following =
      userId &&
      (await Follower.findOne({
        "_id.userId": authorId,
        "_id.followerId": userId,
      }).lean());

    toAppend.author.following = loggedUser ? !!following : false;

    const followersCount = await Follower.countDocuments({
      "_id.userId": authorId,
    });
    toAppend.author.followersCount = followersCount;
  } else {
    const following =
      userId &&
      (await Follower.findOne({
        "_id.userId": toAppend._id,
        "_id.followerId": userId,
      }).lean());

    toAppend.following = loggedUser ? !!following : false;

    const followersCount = await Follower.countDocuments({
      "_id.userId": toAppend._id,
    });
    toAppend.followersCount = followersCount;
  }
};

const articleResponse = async (articleDoc, loggedUser) => {
  const article = articleDoc;
  const authorDoc = await User.findById(article.authorId).lean();

  let following = false;
  if (loggedUser && authorDoc) {
    const follow = await Follower.findOne({
      "_id.userId": authorDoc._id,
      "_id.followerId": loggedUser._id,
    }).lean();
    following = !!follow;
  }

  let favorited = false;
  if (loggedUser) {
    const fav = await Favorite.findOne({
      "_id.articleId": article._id,
      "_id.userId": loggedUser._id,
    }).lean();
    favorited = !!fav;
  }

  return {
    slug: article.slug,
    title: article.title,
    description: article.description,
    body: article.body,
    createdAt: article.createdAt,
    updatedAt: article.updatedAt,
    tagList: Array.isArray(article.tagList) ? [...article.tagList] : [],
    favorited,
    favoritesCount: article.favoritesCount ?? 0,
    author: {
      username: authorDoc ? authorDoc.username : null,
      bio: authorDoc ? authorDoc.bio : null,
      image: authorDoc ? authorDoc.image : null,
      following,
      followersCount: authorDoc ? (authorDoc.followersCount ?? 0) : 0,
    },
  };
};

module.exports = {
  slugify,
  appendTagList,
  appendFavorites,
  appendFollowers,
  articleResponse,
};
```
